0. Definitions

"The Library" means the rayo runtime as released by its copyright holders:
the files under include/, src/, lib/ and hook/ of the rayo repository
(https://github.com/pesaclarity/rayo), and the libraries and the Dart
package (package:rayo) built from them. rayo-convert (convert/), the tests,
the tools and the examples are not part of the Library.

"The Public API" means the functions, types, constants and macros declared
in the headers under include/rayo/, and the Dart declarations exported by
lib/rayo.dart, as documented in those files and in docs/.

"A Permitted Configuration" of the Library is the Library with no change to
its source files other than:

  a) setting the compile-time options that include/rayo/config.h documents,
     or the macros the documentation names for choosing a platform layer
     or kernels (such as RAYO_NO_PLATFORM);
  b) building it with any compiler, flags, linker or build system, for any
     target, as a static library, a shared library or as object files; and
  c) extending it only through the Public API, such as ops of your own
     given to rayo_model_create_with through include/rayo/op.h.

"An Application" means a work that uses the Library only through the Public
API, and that contains no part of the Library other than what including the
Library's headers or importing package:rayo puts in it.

"A Combined Work" means an Application linked with, or packaged together
with, the Library in a Permitted Configuration, statically or dynamically,
in one executable or in one package (such as an Android APK or App Bundle,
an iOS or macOS app, or a desktop program and its libraries).

